From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 120/159] ASoC: codecs: Add Awinic AW882xx amplifier driver

Add a driver for the Awinic smart power amplifier with chip ID 0x1852,
used for the loudspeaker of the Moto G 5G Plus on secondary MI2S. It
is not one of the AW88xxx parts already supported upstream.

The amplifier is configured from the register table the vendor ships
as firmware (pairs of little-endian 16-bit register addresses and
values), with the current/voltage sensing gain set from the efuses.
It stays powered down and hard-muted until a stream is unmuted, then
waits for its PLL to lock on the I2S clocks before unmuting.

Controls:
 - Playback Volume: 0.5 dB steps from -90 dB to 0 dB, written to the
   attenuation field of HAGCCFG4 (6 dB and 0.5 dB nibbles).
 - Channel Select: left, right or (L + R) / 2; the default is the
   average, as there is a single speaker.

Like the downstream driver, a monitor running every 3 s while playing
reads the battery voltage (averaged) and the die temperature and adds
attenuation and lowers the boost peak current below thresholds, with
hysteresis. The thresholds are those of the Motorola device tree; the
peak current is only ever lowered from the value of the register
table. The DSP-side limit (VMAX) of the downstream speaker protection
is not implemented, nor is the speaker protection itself.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
